Article 5 Where a lessor concludes several lease contracts for the same house, and when all the contracts are valid, if all lessees claim performance of the contract, the People's Court shall determine the lessee to whom the contract shall be performed in accordance with the following order:
(1) the lessee who has lawfully taken possession of the leased house;
(2) the lessee who has completed the registration and filing procedures;
(3) the lessee whose contract was concluded earlier.
If a lessee who is unable to obtain the leased house requests dissolution of the contract and compensation for losses, the matter shall be handled in accordance with the relevant provisions of the Civil Code.

Article 9 Where a lessee, with the lessor's consent, decorates or refurbishes the house, and the contract is dissolved, and the parties have no agreement on the disposal of the affixed decoration or refurbishment items, the People's Court shall handle the matter respectively according to the following circumstances:
(1) where the contract is dissolved due to the lessor's breach of contract, and the lessee requests the lessor to compensate for the residual value loss of the decoration or refurbishment during the remaining lease term, the request shall be supported;
(2) where the contract is dissolved due to the lessee's breach of contract, and the lessee requests the lessor to compensate for the residual value loss of the decoration or refurbishment during the remaining lease term, the request shall not be supported. However, if the lessor agrees to utilize the items, the lessor shall make appropriate compensation within the scope of the utilization value;
(3) where the contract is dissolved due to breach of contract by both parties, the residual value loss of the decoration or refurbishment during the remaining lease term shall be borne by both parties according to their respective fault;
(4) where the contract is dissolved due to reasons not attributable to either party, the residual value loss of the decoration or refurbishment during the remaining lease term shall be shared by both parties in accordance with the principle of fairness. Where laws provide otherwise, their provisions shall apply.

Article 12 Where a lessee extends the construction with the lessor's consent, but the parties have no agreement on the disposal of the extension costs, the People's Court shall handle the matter respectively according to the following circumstances:
(1) where the legal construction procedures have been completed, the construction cost of the extension shall be borne by the lessor;
(2) where the legal construction procedures have not been completed, the construction cost of the extension shall be shared by both parties according to fault.
